from ./Access import Limits, ResetDefences
from ./Failures import OperatorAlerts

export anchor Admin:
    who:
        The operator is the person who runs NameTempest. The operator is a
        role on an account, granted by hand in the database. A customer can
        never reach the admin interface, and there is no way to grant
        yourself the role from inside the product.
    scope:
        The admin interface sets limits and fixes people. It does not take
        payments, issue refunds or change a bill, because the payment
        provider does that.
    limits:
        Every value under @{Limits}: the free allowance, what each plan
        gets, the number of names in a round, and what each effort level
        costs. A change is confirmed before it is saved and takes effect on
        the next counted action.
    freeUseCeiling:
        The ceiling on free use per network address, described under
        @{ResetDefences}. It is a setting like every other limit, and the
        operator can raise it when a shared address is wrongly caught.
    models:
        Which model each effort level uses, and whether a level is
        available. A change is confirmed before it is saved.
    style:
        The pick lists behind the naming style form: the choices in the
        naming style and tone lists. A choice that is removed stops being
        offered, and no existing project loses the style it already holds.
    lookup:
        Whether a paid domain lookup service is used, and which one. The
        shipped chain needs no subscription, so this is empty until the
        operator adds a service.
    prices:
        The monthly price of Pro, the per-seat price of Studio, and the
        size and price of credit packs. A price change applies to new
        purchases and to the next renewal, never to a bill already paid.
    people:
        Search for an account by email address and see its plan, its
        organization, its seats, its remaining allowance this month and its
        credits. The operator can grant credits, change a plan, and remove a
        person from an organization, with a reason recorded.
    seats:
        Add or remove a seat on an organization when a customer cannot, so
        a studio is never stuck below its needed seats.
    audit:
        Every admin change records what changed, the old and the new value,
        the time, the operator and the reason. The record cannot be edited
        from the interface.
    alerts:
        Alerts raised by a repeated failure, described under
        @{OperatorAlerts}, newest first. The operator dismisses an alert,
        reads its detail, or marks a part unavailable from it.
    safeguards:
        A value that is not a positive whole number is refused with a
        plain message. A change never leaves an organization with fewer
        seats than members. Clearing a limit is a separate, explicit
        action, never a side effect of an empty field.
    access:
        Removing the operator role ends every open admin session. An admin
        action that touches a customer is announced to that customer by
        email when it changes what they paid for.
